+## 🔎 Observed boundary and repair
+
+The declaration was committed locally as
+`d98f7d6b22459b4a9aa7306ab054c8e09e02e5d0` before the single dispatch probe.
+[The retained probe](evidence/SPN-149/playwright-boundary-probe.ts) executed the
+actual pinned Playwright `FrameManager` methods with a synthetic page/context;
+it did not launch a browser or a Spinel server. Source SHA-256:
+`6b7adcb0a697b1f6db276e61a559efced37a0f7a8b68e9fcbbc0d425c67c561a`.
+[Result](evidence/SPN-149/boundary-probe-result.json): one established socket and
+one page close event for close-before-clearing; one established socket and zero
+page close events for clearing-before-close. Both declared orderings completed
+in one process, 637 ms including the serial runner, peak 221,928 KiB.
+
+This demonstrates a conditional observation defect in the installed dependency.
+It does **not** establish that the original failed browser attempt had this
+ordering, or that server revocation failed. The
+[original case](evidence/SPN-149/original-13557930894-case.json),
+[DOM limitation](evidence/SPN-149/original-13557930894-error-context-summary.json),
+and [pinned source provenance](evidence/SPN-149/original-13557930894-playwright-source.json)
+remain separate. The original artifact's actual retention was seven days,
+expiring 2026-11-14 02:54:57 UTC; PR #268's 30-day statement was incorrect.
+Reviewed content-free extracts and member hashes now survive that expiry.
+The missing first-attempt socket/session/navigation timeline remains unavailable.
+
+Agent decision: use the supported Chromium CDP Network event interface in
+`e2e/session-revocation.ts`, installed before navigation, without modifying
+application/session/transport code or intercepting the revoked socket. Pin the
+observed request IDs privately until cleanup, require a real 101 establishment,
+and freeze all open matching sockets immediately before the synchronous session
+revocation. Only their actual protocol close events count. The observer also
+rejects a later established connection, observer loss and diagnostic overflow.
+Main-frame navigation and legacy page close events are diagnostic events only.
+
+The existing journey retains independent 401 denial, sign-in/editor removal,
+surviving socket continuity, successful forwarded queued writes and saved native
+content. It now verifies the same native cell after reload and rejects **any**
+later matching socket frame, without retaining frame payloads. The timeline has
+at most 64 finite events and 16 sockets; overflow fails closed. Every attempt
+attaches the content-free timeline, source/runtime fields and cleanup disposition,
+including when its first assertion fails. Cleanup releases held writes, detaches
+the owned observer, closes the owned context and removes disposable database
+state. Each phase has a five-second cleanup bound inside the unchanged test
+deadline; later phases still run after a rejection, and cleanup/attachment errors
+cannot replace the primary test failure.
